{"assets":[],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"1796","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"A. Typical Interview Problem"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"2 seconds"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"512 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The FB-string is formed as follows. Initially, it is empty. We go through all positive integers, starting from $$$1$$$, in ascending order, and do the following for each integer:"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":false},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" if the current integer is divisible by $$$3$$$, append "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"F"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" to the end of the FB-string; "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" if the current integer is divisible by $$$5$$$, append "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"B"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" to the end of the FB-string. "}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note that if an integer is divisible by both $$$3$$$ and $$$5$$$, we append "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"F"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":", and then "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"B"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":", not in the opposite order."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first $$$10$$$ characters of the FB-string are "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"FBFFBFFBFB"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":": the first "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"F"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" comes from the integer $$$3$$$, the next character ("},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"B"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":") comes from $$$5$$$, the next "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"F"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" comes from the integer $$$6$$$, and so on. It's easy to see that this string is infinitely long. Let $$$f_i$$$ be the $$$i$$$-th character of FB-string; so, $$$f_1$$$ is "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"F"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":", $$$f_2$$$ is "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"B"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":", $$$f_3$$$ is "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"F"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":", $$$f_4$$$ is "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"F"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":", and so on."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"You are given a string $$$s$$$, consisting of characters "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"F"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" and/or "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"B"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":". You have to determine whether it is a substring (contiguous subsequence) of the FB-string. In other words, determine if it is possible to choose two integers $$$l$$$ and $$$r$$$ ($$$1 \\le l \\le r$$$) so that the string $$$f_l f_{l+1} f_{l+2} \\dots f_r$$$ is exactly $$$s$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"For example:"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":false},"children":[{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"FFB"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" is a substring of the FB-string: if we pick $$$l = 3$$$ and $$$r = 5$$$, the string $$$f_3 f_4 f_5$$$ is exactly "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"FFB"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"; "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"BFFBFFBF"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" is a substring of the FB-string: if we pick $$$l = 2$$$ and $$$r = 9$$$, the string $$$f_2 f_3 f_4 \\dots f_9$$$ is exactly "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"BFFBFFBF"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"; "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"BBB"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" is not a substring of the FB-string. "}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line contains one integer $$$t$$$ ($$$1 \\le t \\le 2046$$$) — the number of test cases."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Each test case consists of two lines. The first line contains one integer $$$k$$$ ($$$1 \\le k \\le 10$$$) — the number of characters in $$$s$$$. The second line contains $$$s$$$, which is a string of exactly $$$k$$$ characters. Each character of $$$s$$$ is either "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"F"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" or "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"B"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"For each test case, print "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"YES"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" if $$$s$$$ is a substring of the FB-string, or "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"NO"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" otherwise."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"You may print each letter in any case ("},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"YES"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"yes"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Yes"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" will all be recognized as positive answer, "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"NO"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"no"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" and "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"nO"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" will all be recognized as negative answer)."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Example"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n3\n3\nFFB\n8\nBFFBFFBF\n3\nBBB\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\nYES\nYES\nNO\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"document"},"index":"A","problemCode":"1796A","schema":2,"sourceKind":"html","sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/contest/1796/problem/A"}